./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:1:# Agent Notes contract
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:3:Agent Notes are effectively RFCs written by agents: durable proposals and decision records that preserve the rationale, the alternatives, the consequences and the required verification that code, tests and ordinary documentation cannot carry. They exist so a later session can find out why a decision was made and what it beat before it re-opens the question.
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:12:  - **`proposed/`** — proposals reviewed before implementation; not yet built, or only partly.
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:48:An implemented note that is fully superseded may be consolidated into the current owning note and deleted. Before deletion the owner must preserve every unique rationale, alternative, consequence, required verification and named coverage gap; repair every inbound link; and delete the old note and its companions in the same change. Partial supersession does not qualify: keep both notes cross-linked and update every fact that remains current. Consolidation must not rewrite the old file into its opposite or rely on the project's history as the only copy of the rationale.
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:61:# Agent Note: <title>
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:116:<!-- agent-note-format: alternatives-not-recorded (pre-format Agent Note) -->
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:127:A note is the source member of a unit. The unit also contains every companion assigned to that note: translations, consistency records, diagrams or other supporting files. Repeated `--companion <suffix>` arguments classify same-stem companions. Repeated `--member <source>=<companion>` arguments declare exact membership when the mechanism uses another stem or nested path. Check paths are relative to the notes root; archive paths are relative to the archive root. A companion stays under the source's class, and an active member also stays under the same lifecycle. Neither form requires every note to have every possible companion. Notes are written for the agent in English; translations are optional reader companions.
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:129:An external mechanism owns a companion's naming convention, content, consistency records and validation. Agent Notes does not assume a translation format, target code, aggregate record or particular skill. The responsible model discovers the project's mechanism and resolves the current unit's members; the scripts receive those facts as parameters.
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:141:An existing translation workflow may require separate production and review. If that separation is unavailable, do not translate in the working context: keep the source note, report the selected targets as pending unit members, and hand over the missing mechanism with a resumable next step.
./.agents/skills/dsh-spec-agent-notes/references/notes-contract.md:145:Companions form one unit with their note: they are moved, sealed and deleted together. The format gate reports a suffix-classified companion without a source and validates every path-scoped member source and companion as regular, contained files. The owning mechanism checks internal consistency. Seal preparation records the exact members expected for each new unit; seal-time completeness applies that unit's expected set, not a global target union. Verification does not replay the expectation over frozen history.
